course: dictionary
lesson: 15485
title: Stripping and its clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Stripping means taking something off, such as a covering or a layer. The clues in the sentence tell you what is being taken off. «Dad is stripping the old wallpaper from the kitchen wall.» Dad is pulling the paper off the wall, so stripping means removing a layer.
explain: The same idea works with other things. «We stripped the beds and put the sheets in the wash.» Stripping the beds means taking the sheets off to wash them. «The wind was stripping the leaves from the trees.» Here the wind pulls the leaves away.
explain: To check your meaning, ask yourself: what is being taken off? Paper, sheets, leaves, or clothes? Then put your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Stripping is the -ing form of the verb strip.
fact: «Stripping» can mean taking off a covering or layer, like wallpaper, paint, or sheets.
fact: «Stripped of» means taken away officially, as when a cheating winner is stripped of a medal.
fact: Useful phrases are «strip the bed», «strip off», and «strip away».
fact: «Stripping» can also mean taking off your clothes, for example for a doctor's check-up or a swim.
exercise: «Dad is stripping the old wallpaper off the kitchen wall.» What is Dad doing? | Washing the wall with soap | Painting a new picture on the wall | Hanging up a clock | *Taking off a layer from the wall
exercise: «The runner was stripped of her medal after she cheated.» What does stripped of mean here? | Put on a shiny new medal | Given a big gold prize | *Taken away officially | Lost in the race
exercise: «We stripped the beds and put the sheets in the wash.» What did we do to the beds? | Made them very tidy | Put new sheets on them | *Took the sheets off them | Jumped on them
test: «The wind was stripping the leaves from the trees.» What is the wind doing to the leaves? | Painting them gold | Blowing them into bright colours | *Pulling them away | Making them grow
test: «Mum showed me how to strip away the old paint.» What does strip away mean? | Leave the paint alone | *Remove the paint layer by layer | Add more paint on top | Mix the paint with water
exam: The nurse said, «Please start stripping for your check-up.» What does stripping mean here? | Walking to the door | Ringing a bell | Shouting loudly | *Taking off your clothes
